+## Follow-up deep dive: systemic fake content in 9 language courses
+
+Prompted by a request to verify every lesson/quiz/exam across Fearn is
+distinct and has substantial content, I scanned all 29 curricula files
+for duplicate/generic text at scale (not just the boilerplate-prefix
+pattern already fixed above). Result:
+
+**Amharic, Cantonese, French, Hindi, Korean, Mandarin, Swahili,
+Ukrainian, and Urdu — 850 lessons each, ~7,600+ lessons combined — are
+not real lesson content.** Verified directly by reading raw lesson
+objects (not just counting duplicates). Example: Mandarin lesson
+`zh-u1-l1`, objective "Comprehensive mastery of 汉语拼音与日常问候
+(Pinyin & Basic Greetings)":
+
+- `presentation.explanation` — generic template sentence restating the
+  lesson title, no real grammar content.
+- `presentation.examples` — three sentences about a teacher explaining
+  syntax in a media classroom, borrowing academic journals from a
+  library, and a city's transit network — **none relate to greetings or
+  pinyin**, the lesson's actual topic.
+- `presentation.mnemonics` — literally the string `"Key cognitive anchor
+  for 汉语拼音与日常问候 (Pinyin & Basic Greetings)"`, not an actual
+  mnemonic.
+- `presentation.culturalNotes` — literally `"Cultural nuance and
+  communicative etiquette in Mandarin."` for every lesson.
+- `checkpointTest` multiple-choice item — asks about the lesson's
+  grammar, but the three answer options are unrelated filler sentences
+  (a UN summit declaration, high-speed rail punctuality, an AI/quantum
+  computing conference) with no connection to the lesson topic, so the
+  "correct" answer is arbitrary rather than testing anything real.
+- `checkpointTest` typed-recall item — asks the learner to type
+  `你好_1_1`, a raw internal disambiguation ID leaking into user-facing
+  text instead of the clean word `你好`.
+
+Confirmed the identical failure shape (generic mismatched explanation +
+mismatched examples + fake mnemonic/cultural-notes placeholders + fake
+quiz distractors + leaked `word_N_N` IDs) recurs across all 9 languages,
+850 lessons apiece, and is absent from the other 20 subjects (Japanese,
+Spanish, German, Turkish, English, etc. — those are genuinely authored,
+aside from the boilerplate-prefix issue already fixed above). Also
+confirmed each of these 9 languages' `.ledger.js` file falsely claims
+every lesson is `"authoredInFull"` with `"stubOnly": []` — the app has no
+internal record that this content isn't real, so it presents as complete
+courses.
+
+**Disposition:** raised this with the user directly. Given the scale
+(properly fixing this means authoring ~7,600 real, on-topic lessons
+across 9 languages — a large content project, not a mechanical bug fix),
+they asked to leave the content as-is for now and just have it
+documented here. Not touched in this session.
+
